course: dictionary
lesson: 15845
title: Undivided
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Undivided is built from three parts: un- means not, divide means to split, and -ed shows it describes something. So undivided means not split up. When someone gives you undivided attention, all of their focus is on you, with none of it shared with anything else. «I need your undivided attention, please.» The teacher wants you to stop looking out of the window and focus on her.
explain: The second meaning is about things. Something undivided is whole, in one piece. «The field was undivided, with no fences at all.» Here the field is one large space, not cut into smaller pieces.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «Mum gave her undivided attention to my story.» If you swap in "shared", the sentence no longer makes sense, so undivided means complete and given to one thing only.
fact: Undivided means not split up or shared.
fact: «Undivided attention» means giving your full focus to one thing.
fact: The prefix un- often means not, as in unkind, unfair and undivided.
fact: «Undivided loyalty» means being fully faithful, with none of it given to anyone else.
fact: In civics, «one nation, indivisible» means one whole country that cannot be split.
exercise: «I need your undivided attention.» What does undivided mean here? | Noisy and loud | *Complete, with all your focus on one thing | Shared between many things | Lost or missing
exercise: Which phrase means whole and not split into parts? | a broken promise | *an undivided country | a shared pizza | a divided vote
exercise: «The field was undivided, with no fences at all.» Find and copy the word that means not split up. | with | field | fences | *undivided
test: «Ben gave the puzzle his undivided attention.» What does this tell us? | Ben shared the puzzle with three friends | Ben lost the puzzle pieces | Ben did the puzzle quickly and carelessly | *Ben focused completely on the puzzle
test: Which word is closest in meaning to undivided? | Hidden | *Whole | Broken | Scattered
exam: The word undivided is made from un- and divide. What does un- mean here? | *Not | Under | Very much | Again
